A||||42||fieroburton||i need your all's openion||||4||
Z||000000||fieroburton||08-23-2001||10:47 AM||||just got back from midas and they told me i needed :<BR>front=<BR>2 front calapers<BR>rotors<BR>hoses<BR>brake pads<P>rear=<BR>2 rear callapers <BR>rotors <BR>hoses<BR>brake cables<BR>bleed and flush<P>that totaled $1,733 <BR>im asking all of you , do you think its worth doing ? i got the car for $1,200<BR>do all of you think i should get the it fixed or should i sell the car to a fiero inthosiest that is willing to do the work and get a better one ?<BR>or should i go to another auto service to get a quote ? <BR><P>------------------<BR>1984 2M4 SE <BR>         <IMG SRC="http://publish.hometown.aol.com/fieroburton/myhomepage/07_07.jpg?mtbrand=AOL_US">     [URL=http://www.geocities.com/fieroburton/1.html]||||reg||4
Z||000001||CoolBlue87GT||08-23-2001||11:00 AM||||Ouch !  I'd go talk with the Pontiac Dealer, and let them check it over, and suggest what it needs. Or try another company.<P>I wouldn't tell them about the quote you were given.  <P>Luckly my dealer is a Fiero lover & can be trusted.<P>The car looks to be in good shape. The repair quote sounds to high, but brakes are something you don't want to scrimp on.<P>Good luck.<P>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/1cool.jpg">  <BR><p>[This message has been edited by CoolBlue87GT (edited 08-23-2001).]||||reg||6
Z||000002||MinnGreenGT||08-23-2001||11:04 AM||||It's not what you paid for the car, but what the car is worth to you! I've easily got $10k into my car (had it for 6 years this month). There is no way I'd get rid of it- unless truly necessary.  As for the cost of brakes- can you do it yourself? or do you know anyone mechanically inclined that you can buy a case of beer for in payment (many auto repairs have been done over a case).  Check out the <A HREF="http://www.angelfire.com/biz/fierosails/info.html" TARGET=_blank>Fiero Secrets </A> website for info on brake replacements and upgrades. Good Luck!<P>------------------<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/grngtsig3.jpg">      <P>Medium Metallic Green 87 GT<BR>3.1L High Output<BR>4 Spd OD Tranny<BR>Open (read: Loud) Exhaust<BR>and More!<BR>-Rob Bartlett<p>[This message has been edited by MinnGreenGT (edited 08-23-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000003||TONY_C||08-23-2001||11:09 AM||||Midas is trying to hose you.  you're looking at around $400 in parts including wheel bearing and seals which they didnt mention.  i can't see how they can have the nerve to quote you $1700 for brakes.  shop around. you should be able to do much better than that.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Oreif||08-23-2001||11:11 AM||||Well <B>IF</B> you <I>REALLY</I> need all those parts, It's about $524.00 for the parts. (current NAPA prices) So the rest would be labor. At $65 per hour for labor (which is about the average) That works out to be 18.6 hours to do it!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_bs.gif">  It's called "A rip-off"!! Two years ago I re-did my suspension and brakes. Using a hydralic jack and 2 jackstands I was able to replace everything you listed above in about 6 hours by myself. No impact tools and no lift. I would find a more reputable shop or do the work yourself. I doubt you need all of the items listed. You could even save about $200 and just buy the rebuild kits for the calipers instead of new ones.<p>[This message has been edited by Oreif (edited 08-23-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000005||thomas_l||08-23-2001||11:21 AM||||Sounds like a "shotgun" quote to me. You didn't mention why you took it there in the first place. You ought to find a forum member in your area willing to take a look or at least recommend a reputable repair shop for a 2nd opinion. Fact is, you may need all that stuff on your 17 year old car, just not all at once. Try to get shop #2 to prioritize and break that big job into affordable pieces, if it really needs all that work.<P>With respect to replacing the car with another Fiero you will just end up buying someone else's big repair job or paying them more for work already done. I'd say go with the devil you know already.<P>Everyone always gives me a grief about picking up (towing) my 87 GT for $400. It was a great deal until I made it roadworthy with a complete transmission, clutch, rear wheel bearings, brakes, etc etc etc to the point that I have just over $2000 in it now. Besides that, I have the experience and tools to do all that work myself. Not to mention it would take another $2k to make it really useful as a daily driver.||||reg||1
Z||000006||Joe Torma||08-23-2001||11:22 AM||||That's nuts!!!<P>Do you know for sure you need those parts?!<P>I'd help, but I'm nowhere near you, hell you can fly someone in for that $$$.<P>Using the FieroStore's prices...<BR>80+60 for rotors<BR>140+180 for calipers<BR>100 for stainless lines<BR>40 for cables<BR>$600 in parts?!  $1100 in labor?<P>What do they smoke at Midas?<P>Hey, call up pontiac with your VIN #...if you are lucky, thr recall wasn't done, and you could have the rears done for free!!!<p>[This message has been edited by Joe Torma (edited 08-23-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000007||fieroburton||08-23-2001||11:30 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by thomas_l:<BR><B> You didn't mention why you took it there in the first place. </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>took it there because when i got the car (about 5 months ago) the man who i got it from told me to have the brake pads looked at , so i did  and BOOM im up ****  creek !<P>------------------<BR>1984 2M4 SE <BR>         <IMG SRC="http://publish.hometown.aol.com/fieroburton/myhomepage/07_07.jpg?mtbrand=AOL_US">     [URL=http://www.geocities.com/fieroburton/1.html]||||reg||1
Z||000008||84Bill||08-23-2001||11:51 AM||||OMG!!<BR>Junk yard cars need fewer new parts than that!||||reg||11
