Z||000011||fieroburton||08-23-2001||12:57 PM||||so you say to keep the car and have the repares don ? <BR>how well does 84's go up in value or do the value drop every year ?<BR>if i cant sell the car for more than i put in it then to me its not worth doing.<P>------------------<BR>1984 2M4 SE <BR>         <IMG SRC="http://publish.hometown.aol.com/fieroburton/myhomepage/07_07.jpg?mtbrand=AOL_US">     [URL=http://www.geocities.com/fieroburton/1.html]||||reg||1
Z||000012||Tigger||08-23-2001||01:01 PM||||I wouldn't even let them install the pads.<P>I agree with thomas, a 17 year old car needs all those things replaced at one time or another, but not all at one time.  I could see them saying your caliper slides are bunged up and it would be a good time to get new calipers, but you don't have to replace all of the brake lines, parking brake cables and everything else at the same time.  My goodness I can't believe he left the brake master cylinder and porportioning valve off the list.  I would definetely get another quote from another shop.<P>$1,733  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif"><P>||||reg||1
Z||000013||fieroburton||08-23-2001||01:09 PM||||he showed me the dammage and they do need replaced  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"> the brake lines are cracking and the e brake does not work because the wire or somthing is broke in two . and you can see it hanging loos under the car.<BR>im just thinking, 1 were do i get the money 2 how do i get it fixed cheaper 3 should i even keep the car ||||reg||1
Z||000014||Oreif||08-23-2001||01:13 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by fieroburton:<BR><B>so you say to keep the car and have the repares don ? <BR>how well does 84's go up in value or do the value drop every year ?<BR>if i cant sell the car for more than i put in it then to me its not worth doing.<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><BR>Fiero prices have basically "bottomed out" So every year that passes they go up in value. The increase isn't anything to brag about. A fully loaded 84 SE has increased in price by $100 in the past 3 years. Keeping the car in excellent condition, (Clean, and all things working), will always help to increase it's value.  Just remember that even though the prices always increase, It'll never skyrocket to some silly value.<BR>Don't use the car as a retirement asset.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000015||mrfixit58||08-23-2001||01:50 PM||||If you can make it to Florida, I'll do it for half that!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"> Seriously, those guys were trying to hose you. My sister-in-law was almost in tears last year when some "chain" store told her it would cost $650 to re-do her front brakes. They said she needed rotors, calipers, hoses, pads, etc. and it was leaking brake fluid. I told her to bring it over and I'd take a look at it. <P>What I found was that, when they (same chain store) replaced her pads a year earlier, they didn't lubricate the slide pins. This caused the inside pad on the drivers side to wear out prematurely. I replaced the pads, lubed the pins and for $25 and an hour later she was on her way. It would have cost less but she insisted on buying me enough oil for my next oil change. <P>The point of this story is to let you know your not alone. My advise, find someone you trust who has a little mechanical knowledge and ask them to help YOU do the brake job. You'll learn a bunch and gain a lot of confidence. If you can't find someone to help, shop around. <BR><P>------------------<BR>Roy :D<BR>87 GT   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/pennocksize.JPG"> ||||reg||6
Z||000016||Tigger||08-23-2001||01:53 PM||||The decision on keeping the car depends on a lot of other factors.<P>I'd still get a second quote from another shop to do the work before giving up.<P>The cheapest method would be to buy the parts you need to replace now and do the work yourself and with the help of a friend if you haven't done brake work before (Mt dew and Pizza works for me, just wish I lived closer).  Is this your primary car?<p>[This message has been edited by Tigger (edited 08-23-2001).]||||reg||1
